{"files":[{"content":"#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <limits.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float distance;\n    unsigned int encounter;\n    char label;\n} Neighbor;\n\nstatic inline int neighbor_is_worse(const Neighbor *a, const Neighbor *b) {\n    return a->distance > b->distance ||\n           (a->distance == b->distance && a->encounter > b->encounter);\n}\n\nstatic void sift_up_worst(Neighbor *neighbors, int index) {\n    Neighbor value = neighbors[index];\n\n    while (index > 0) {\n        int parent = (index - 1) / 2;\n        if (!neighbor_is_worse(&value, &neighbors[parent])) {\n            break;\n        }\n        neighbors[index] = neighbors[parent];\n        index = parent;\n    }\n\n    neighbors[index] = value;\n}\n\nstatic void sift_down_worst(Neighbor *neighbors, int length) {\n    Neighbor value = neighbors[0];\n    int parent = 0;\n\n    for (;;) {\n        int child = parent * 2 + 1;\n        if (child >= length) {\n            break;\n        }\n\n        int right = child + 1;\n        if (right < length && neighbor_is_worse(&neighbors[right], &neighbors[child])) {\n            child = right;\n        }\n        if (!neighbor_is_worse(&neighbors[child], &value)) {\n            break;\n        }\n\n        neighbors[parent] = neighbors[child];\n        parent = child;\n    }\n\n    neighbors[parent] = value;\n}\n\nstatic char knn_insertion(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char *labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(*labels) * (size_t) k);\n    float *distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(*distances) * (size_t) k);\n    int i, j, x, y;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n                    for (y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                        distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                        labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                    }\n\n                    distances[x] = d;\n                    labels[x] = g.label;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(*labels), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    Neighbor *neighbors = (Neighbor *) malloc(sizeof(*neighbors) * (size_t) k);\n    int count = 0;\n    unsigned int encounter = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n            if (d != d) {\n                free(neighbors);\n                return knn_insertion(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate);\n            }\n\n            Neighbor candidate;\n            candidate.distance = d;\n            candidate.encounter = encounter++;\n            candidate.label = g.label;\n\n            if (count < k) {\n                neighbors[count] = candidate;\n                sift_up_worst(neighbors, count);\n                count++;\n            } else if (d < neighbors[0].distance) {\n                neighbors[0] = candidate;\n                sift_down_worst(neighbors, count);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    while (count < k) {\n        neighbors[count].label = -1;\n        count++;\n    }\n\n    int frequencies[UCHAR_MAX + 1] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        frequencies[(unsigned char) neighbors[i].label]++;\n    }\n\n    char most_frequent = 0;\n    int most_frequent_count = 0;\n    for (int value = CHAR_MIN; value <= CHAR_MAX; value++) {\n        char label = (char) value;\n        int frequency = frequencies[(unsigned char) label];\n        if (frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = label;\n            most_frequent_count = frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(neighbors);\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n","path":"src/knn.c"}],"hypothesis":"A contiguous max-heap removes the O(k) tail shift for each accepted point while retaining the baseline's strict-distance and encounter-order top-k semantics; direct byte-label frequency counting also avoids sorting the selected labels.","notes":"The NaN fallback retains the original insertion behavior for unordered floating-point distances. Equal-distance heap priority evicts the later encounter first, matching the original stable insertion order.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace the sorted top-k arrays with a contiguous bounded max-heap keyed by distance and encounter order.","Replace selected-label qsort voting with a fixed character-frequency scan that preserves the original character-order tie rule."]}